  clock: 1  # b57b
  nonce: b57b  # b57b
  data:  # b57b
    kind: work_item  # b57b
    title: "Agent: always capture full command output to file, never pipe through tail/head"  # b57b
    status: todo_soft  # b57b
    priority: 2  # b57b
    parent:  # b57b
    tags:  # b57b
    - agent-behavior  # b57b
    - dx  # b57b
    before: []  # b57b
    duplicate_of: []  # b57b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b57b
    pr_ref:  # b57b
    description: "## Problem\n\nWhen running long commands (release-check, bakeoff, CI debug), the agent\nfrequently pipes output through `| tail -30` or `| head -20`, losing\nthe full output. When the truncated output doesn't contain the needed\ninformation, the agent re-runs the command (often 5-15 minutes) with a\ndifferent truncation, which may also miss. This has happened repeatedly\nand wastes significant wall-clock time.\n\n## Required Behavior\n\n1. Always redirect full output to a file: `cmd > /tmp/foo.log 2>&1`\n2. Then read the file with the Read tool or targeted grep\n3. As a safety valve against runaway output, use `head -100000` (100K\n   lines ≈ 5-10MB) if there's concern about infinite loops\n4. Never use `| tail -N` as the primary output capture for commands\n   that take more than a few seconds\n\n## Where to Codify\n\nThis should be added to AGENTS.md in a \"Command Output Capture\" section,\nor as a rule in the \"Running Tests (smart-test)\" section. It applies to\nall long-running commands, not just tests.\n\n## Examples of Wasted Time\n\n- release-check took 15 minutes, output lost to `| tail -30`, had to\n  re-run with `> /tmp/file.log 2>&1` (another 15 minutes)\n- CI debug logs piped through grep that missed the relevant lines\n- smart-test manifest generation output lost, had to re-run"  # b57b
    fields: {}  # b57b
